{"overview":"A father, anxious for his son's financial well being, develops a special soda pop called Dopokoke which is laced with cocaine. Dopokoke is advertised as relief \"for that tired feeling.\" The drink is a success, but the son becomes addicted to it, much to his father's regret. Loosely based on the allegations that the Coca-Cola company and other soft drink manufacturers laced their soda with dope.","cast":[{"n":"Charles Hill Mailes","c":"The Father, a Physician","p":"/At3GtUXi9WLKero09JGxxVCY6Ph.jpg","q":"Q731452"},{"n":"Charles West","c":"The Son","p":"/b83aIQMnrWmXxnYm5vbPI1izN7u.jpg","q":"Q738864"},{"n":"Blanche Sweet","c":"The Son's Fiancée","p":"/xlcBzlENawXKPIQnpORlUCNkHmj.jpg","q":"Q267718"},{"n":"Dorothy Bernard","c":"The Secretary","p":"/Aw51i2Azw2IICVyS8zpZE0VqFf6.jpg","q":"Q325971"},{"n":"Robert Harron","c":"At Soda Fountain","p":"/8uqveFAwItcd5Ty2OEMPM37bbZb.jpg","q":"Q1344716"},{"n":"Dell Henderson","c":"Dopokoke Factory Employee (uncredited)","p":"/gA4BPbRHPSvI16n1QcRlAd3gmSo.jpg","q":"Q3021715"},{"n":"Walter Hiers","c":"At Soda Fountain (uncredited)","p":"/u0OR95aRdkx4BdT91k3bF6itiGl.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Alfred Paget","c":"Dopokoke Factory Employee (uncredited)","p":"/rGXy9gRwMRb6GhU8bQeReH56hsJ.jpg","q":"Q629304"},{"n":"Kate Toncray","c":"At Soda Fountain (uncredited)","p":"/qb3ty4jC8UdZrvwjVHIilGjY4kr.jpg","q":"Q3193983"},{"n":"Grace Henderson","c":"The Landlady","p":"/h9DRMmxkbujKEBV4wKyS7hF5nqm.jpg","q":"Q3113003"}],"country":["United States"],"wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/For_His_Son","qid":"Q3747877","rel":{"US":{"d":"1912-01-21","c":"NR"}},"stills":["silent-for-his-son_1.webp","silent-for-his-son_2.webp","silent-for-his-son_3.webp","silent-for-his-son_4.webp"]}